  "final_answer_text": "For the Otter USV, there are two sensor plugins that plausibly serve \"position tracking\":\n\n1. **`gps`** (domain: `ABSOLUTE_POSITIONING`) — raw absolute position fix, compact payload.\n2. **`ins-gps-fusion`** (domain: `DERIVED`) — a fused INS/GPS position+attitude estimate, presumably built on top of GPS and IMU internally.\n\n(Note: `imu` is `RELATIVE_POSITIONING` — it tracks attitude/rates, not absolute position, so it doesn't by itself satisfy \"position tracking,\" though it's often paired with GPS for dead-reckoning/fusion.)\n\nSince these two are not identical in purpose, please clarify which you'd like:\n\n- **Option A:** Just `gps` — simplest, lowest sensor cost, raw absolute fixes only.\n- **Option B:** `ins-gps-fusion` only — smoother/more robust fused position estimate (implicitly uses IMU+GPS internally).\n- **Option C:** Both `gps` and `imu` explicitly, plus `ins-gps-fusion` — full raw + fused telemetry (highest sensor cost/data volume).\n\n**If you'd like me to proceed without further input, my default recommendation is Option A (`gps` alone)** — it's the minimal, direct choice for \"position tracking\" and keeps sensor artifact volume/cost low. I can add `imu`/fusion later if you also need heading/attitude tracking or filtered estimates.\n\nLet me know which option you want (A, B, C, or a custom combination), and confirm you want me to build/construct this into an Otter (`vehicle-a-otter`) scenario — I'll also need basic experiment parameters (name, duration, timestep, seed, backend, mission waypoints) if you haven't specified a scenario already.",
